              "type": "text",
              "text": "I fixed the bug in `textutils/wrap.py`, and both tests in `tests/test_wrap.py` now pass. I didn't change the tests.\n\nThe width check was off by one. It used `<`, so it only added a word when the line came out shorter than `width`, and a line that exactly filled `width` was split. For example, `\"aaa bbb\"` at width 7 came out as two lines. I changed the check to `<=` so a line can be exactly `width` characters long, which is what the docstring says it should allow."
